+# Implementation Plan: Quarkus Migration
+
+**Branch**: `[001-quarkus-migration]` | **Date**: 2026-08-26 | **Spec**: specs/001-quarkus-migration/spec.md
+
+**Input**: Feature specification from `/specs/001-quarkus-migration/spec.md`
+
+## Summary
+
+Migrate a Spring Boot 4.0.7 application with a single REST endpoint (`GET /greeting`) to native Quarkus 3.27.3.SP1 (Red Hat BOM). The legacy application consists of 3 Java source files (`GreetingController.java`, `Greeting.java`, `RestServiceApplication.java`) and 1 test file. The migration replaces Spring Boot annotations with JAX-RS equivalents, adopts the Quarkus BOM and Maven plugin, and re-packages from `com.example.restservice` to `com.demo`.
+
+## Technical Context
+
+**Language/Version**: Java 21
+
+**Primary Dependencies**: Red Hat Quarkus BOM 3.27.3.SP1-redhat-00002, `quarkus-rest`, `quarkus-rest-jackson`
+
+**Storage**: N/A (no database)
+
+**Testing**: `mvn -q clean test` with `@QuarkusTest` (Quarkus JUnit5)
+
+**Target Platform**: Linux server (Quarkus JVM mode)
+
+**Project Type**: web-service (REST API)
+
+**Performance Goals**: Sub-100ms response time for greeting endpoint
+
+**Constraints**: No `quarkus-spring-*` extensions (constitution III); REST under `/api/` prefix; `@ApplicationScoped` CDI; constructor injection
+
+**Scale/Scope**: 1 HTTP endpoint, 1 Java record, 1 application class, 1 test class
+
+## Constitution Check
+
+*GATE: Must pass before Phase 0 research. Re-check after Phase 1 design.*
+
+- **I. Red Hat Quarkus platform**: Destination uses `com.redhat.quarkus.platform` BOM 3.27.3.SP1-redhat-00002.
+- **II. Java 21**: Compiler target is Java 21.
+- **III. Native layering**: Package `com.demo`; no `quarkus-spring-*`; `@ApplicationScoped`; constructor injection; REST at `/api/`.
+- **IV. Quality is an input**: Tests ship with code; `@QuarkusTest` in story write-set.
+- **V. Security**: No authz/CSRF changes — legacy has none.
+- **VI. Performance and simplicity (YAGNI)**: No extra config classes, wrapper DTOs, or error taxonomies.
+- **VII. Legacy HTTP contract is immutable**: `GET /greeting` is the only inventory row; destination maps to `GET /api/greeting`. No invented routes.
+
+## Project Structure
+
+### Source Code (repository root)
+
+```text
+src/
+├── main/
+│   └── java/
+│       └── com/
+│           └── demo/
+│               ├── Application.java          # Quarkus bootstrap (replaces RestServiceApplication)
+│               ├── Greeting.java              # Record (migrated from legacy)
+│               └── GreetingResource.java      # JAX-RS resource (replaces GreetingController)
+└── test/
+    └── java/
+        └── com/
+            └── demo/
+                └── GreetingResourceTest.java  # @QuarkusTest (replaces GreetingControllerTests)
+pom.xml                                         # Quarkus BOM + plugins + extensions
+src/main/resources/
+    └── application.properties                  # Quarkus config (quarkus.http.root-path)
+```
+
+**Structure Decision**: Single project, standard Quarkus layout. No modules or multi-module POM.
+
+## Complexity Tracking
+
+No constitution violations. The migration is a straightforward 1:1 endpoint migration with package rename and framework swap.

